WEBVTT

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:23.050
Before I knew it, I abandoned happiness to survive

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:30.190
Lying to myself, I danced clinging on to illusions

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:36.850
At the edge of my vision when I close my eyes

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.840
I was searching for your smile

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:50.210
With our memories fading

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:57.290
We hold on to our dreams and run  Yeah

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:04.190
These feelings that I shut away in my heart

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:11.420
I'll now grasp them again

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:39.090
When the other Yugi lost his duel against Rafael, he lost Yugi's soul.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.930
I know how bad you feel, but sulking doesn't help.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.720
Let's uncover Doma's secrets and recover the captured souls!

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.620
But I'm worried about Haga and Ryuzaki.  They've vanished.

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.010
Did they betray us and join Doma?

00:01:56.830 --> 00:02:02.830
Runaway Train Duel

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.600
We'll go on ahead.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:12.080
Take care of Professor Hopkins and Rebecca.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:13.960
Yeah.  Leave it to me.

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:17.000
We'll catch up when the Professor is healed.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.820
We're counting on you.  We can't do much without the Professor.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.040
I'm going too!

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.120
I'll save my darling!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.390
Stop, Rebecca.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:28.570
But!

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:30.120
That's enough.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.890
Yugi's the one who's suffering the most.

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:45.180
You don't get it, Grandpa!

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.190
Yugi...

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.400
It's time.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.360
See ya.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.680
Take care.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.360
Yugi...

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.500
Hey, Yugi!  Look!

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.100
Isn't it beautiful?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.440
I wonder what Florida's like!

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:53.140
Aww!  I should've brought my swimsuit!

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:59.000
Hey, are you hungry?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.400
Should I see if the dining car is open?

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:10.120
Yugi...

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:24.020
Cheer up, Yugi!

00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:29.310
I know you're hurting, but you can't mourn forever.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.160
Let's all discuss how to get the other Yugi back.  Okay?

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.130
Sorry.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.790
Yugi...

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.870
Nothing you say will work, Anzu.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:55.570
This incident hit Yugi hard.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:57.010
Leave him be.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:06.050
I, Katsuya Jonouchi, will save the other Yugi!

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:08.200
Jonouchi...

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.060
I couldn't stop my dark urges.

00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:21.000
I lost sight of myself.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.210
This will finish it, Rafael.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.100
I tribute Dark Magician Girl!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:30.370
Take this!

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:37.510
As a result...

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:44.850
Don't look at me like that!

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:49.380
Nameless Pharaoh, feel the rage of your monsters!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.900
Guardian Eatos attacks!

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.480
Forbidden Gospel!

00:06:12.990 --> 00:06:14.050
Partner!

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:15.990
Partner!

00:06:15.990 --> 00:06:20.710
I lost something more valuable than my own life.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:25.590
Damn!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:32.200
I'm sorry, partner.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.380
Yugi hasn't come back yet.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.380
Anyway, something's weird.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:45.160
Haven't you noticed?

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:48.820
Yugi's not the only one who hasn't returned.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:53.490
Every passenger in this car is gone.

00:07:21.860 --> 00:07:23.560
Nobody's here too.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.170
What about the next car?

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.430
No one's here either!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.310
Yugi!

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.650
Something's weird with this train!

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:49.480
All the other passengers are gone.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:53.390
Even though we haven't made any stops.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:55.080
This is impossible.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.420
Do you think they're behind this?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:01.400
Wait, Yugi!

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:16.310
Yugi!

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:18.240
Anzu!

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.930
Yugi!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:24.720
Anzu!

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.950
Honda!  Jonouchi!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:28.940
Damn!

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.780
Yugi, we have to stop the train!

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:33.890
Yeah.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.030
Damn!  What's happening?

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:47.470
Did Doma do this?

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:50.410
Yugi...  Anzu...

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:56.010
Who's there?

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:58.650
Dinosaur Ryuzaki!

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:03.920
Phew, it's just you.  Don't scare me!

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.860
Jonouchi, I have business with you.

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.290
Business?

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.230
I'm here for your soul.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:21.540
Anybody there?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:24.470
Please stop the train!

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:26.560
Engineer!  Anyone!

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:27.910
Stop the train!

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.530
Any way to get to the driver's seat?

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.420
Yugi.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.000
This is the only path.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.060
Be careful.

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.720
You're...

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.170
Insector Haga!

00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.610
Haga?  What's he doing here?

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:03.780
Yugi, duel me.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.710
What?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.970
Haga, don't tell me you're...

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:17.320
I'm not the same as I used to be.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.370
That's Doma's!

00:10:27.370 --> 00:10:30.310
Ryuzaki!  You joined them?

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.430
Why did you join Doma?

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.920
To defeat Yugi, of course.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.180
Haga!

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.700
Let's duel, Yugi!

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.900
Wait a sec!

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:01.720
Anzu!

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:03.500
It's dangerous here!

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:07.370
Haga!  Do you know what you're doing?

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:09.600
I won't let you duel!

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:10.210
Anzu!

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:15.090
Ooh, scary!  I like quiet girls better.

00:11:16.550 --> 00:11:17.590
Say what!

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:21.190
Sorry, but I have no business with you.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:23.780
It's with the Nameless Pharaoh!

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:25.330
What?

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:30.290
I heard you have two personalities.

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:35.940
Don't you want to know where the other Yugi is?

00:11:35.940 --> 00:11:37.470
You know?

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.370
Tell me!

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.620
Duel me if you want to know.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:44.260
I'll tell you if you win.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.980
Haga!  You punk!

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.920
Let's duel, Yugi!

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:57.070
Here I go!  Let's duel, Jonouchi!

00:11:57.430 --> 00:12:00.910
You're the one who detached the train!

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:02.600
Why did you do that?

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.540
What happened to Yugi and Anzu?

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:08.970
Yugi?  He's probably dueling Haga.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:11.970
What?  Haga also joined Doma?

00:12:11.970 --> 00:12:14.910
Damn!  Not just Mai, but Haga and Ryuzaki too!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:19.350
I have unfinished business with you, Jonouchi.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:23.780
Let's end it today!

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:30.110
Whatever!  Do you know what it means to join Doma?

00:12:30.110 --> 00:12:32.730
They're trying to destroy the world!

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.930
Be quiet!  I don't care!

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:39.840
I just want to defeat you!

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.530
Standby already!

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:44.170
This is ridiculous.

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:47.400
Let's leave him and go after Yugi.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.110
Yeah.

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.680
I won't let you!  I'm serious!

00:12:50.680 --> 00:12:52.550
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.150
I already have it!

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.330
The Seal of Orichalcos!

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:00.760
Stop, Ryuzaki!

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:04.930
If you use it, the loser will lose his soul!

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.930
I activate The Seal of Orichalcos.

00:13:10.080 --> 00:13:11.560
Don't do it!

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.070
Honda!

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:31.690
I'm overflowing with power!

00:13:32.510 --> 00:13:34.120
Ryuzaki!  How could you!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:38.790
Seriously?  Ryuzaki used it?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:43.310
No one can leave the seal until there's a winner.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.730
And the loser will...

00:13:44.730 --> 00:13:47.730
I told you I was serious.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:51.480
You idiot!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.250
Don't, Yugi!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:06.180
Stay back, Anzu.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:07.190
Yugi...

00:14:07.520 --> 00:14:12.630
Yugi is in no state to have a rational duel.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.560
I'll go first.  I draw.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.500
I'll use this card.

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:24.440
The Seal of Orichalcos!

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:26.640
Tell me, Yugi.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:29.710
How did it feel to use this card?

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:34.110
Did it feel good when your heart's darkness spread throughout your body?

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.050
I'm just kidding.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:42.110
Don't make such a scary face, Yugi.

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:45.230
I'll know how it feels when I use it now.

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:50.660
Don't!  Do you know what'll happen if you use it?

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:53.160
I'm using it because I do know!

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.560
Anzu!

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:10.850
Anzu!

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:16.220
Yugi...

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.680
So this is the power of the Orichalcos!

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:31.040
It's begun.

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:35.480
Yes.  I don't know how well they'll do.

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:39.910
It'll be good if they win and capture the Pharaoh's soul.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:44.400
Even if they lose, we'll still get their souls.

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:51.290
Just wait, partner.  I promise to save you!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:54.740
Come out, Pheromone Wasp!

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:04.640
Due to The Seal of Orichalcos, Pheromone Wasp gains 500 attack points.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:07.640
I set two cards.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.590
I end my turn.

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.130
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:16.750
I summon Obnoxious Celtic Guard!

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:22.080
Here I go, Haga!

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.330
Haga has two set cards.

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:28.760
Don't lose your cool, Yugi!

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:33.050
Obnoxious Celtic Guard attacks Pheromone Wasp!

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:37.860
That won't work!  I flip over my set card!

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:40.410
I activate the trap card, Mimesis!

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.710
Mimesis?

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:46.510
Yes.  When an Insect is attacked...

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:51.120
...I can replace it with a Level 4 or lower monster in my hand.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.020
Mimesis returns Pheromone Wasp to my hand.

00:16:55.020 --> 00:16:58.590
And I Special Summon Parasite Caterpillar!

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:02.030
What?  It changed into Parasite Caterpillar?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.800
I tricked you, Yugi!

00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:13.110
Parasite Caterpillar infects the monster that destroyed it!

00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:21.280
I'll torture you little by little.

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.970
Jonouchi!  I'm willing to risk my life!

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:30.220
If you're a duelist, you'll accept this battle!

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:33.140
Ryuzaki...  Fine!

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:34.840
I'll say nothing more!

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.700
I'll duel you!

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:37.810
Jonouchi!

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.830
But I'm giving it my all!  Got it?

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:43.280
Of course!

00:17:43.280 --> 00:17:45.770
I won't forgive you if you go easy!

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.290
This duel isn't to defeat Ryuzaki.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.960
This duel is to save him!

00:17:53.430 --> 00:17:54.440
Here I go!

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.710
I Special Summon Gilasaurus!

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:03.820
What?  Special Summon?

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:10.260
Yeah.  I'm allowed to Special Summon it!

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.700
Here's another one!

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:15.130
I Special Summon Gilasaurus!

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.840
Another Special Summon?

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:18.570
Jonouchi!

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:20.740
And one more!

00:18:20.980 --> 00:18:23.280
I summon Kaitoptera!

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:28.910
What?  He instantly summoned three monsters!

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:34.100
And Orichalcos's effect raises their attack points by 500!

00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:40.710
You had two monsters to Special Summon in your opening hand?

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:42.530
You're really lucky!

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:46.560
You fool!  You're one to talk - you always rely on luck!

00:18:46.560 --> 00:18:47.970
What?

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.740
He is right.

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:53.040
Honda!  Whose side are you on?

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.640
Sorry.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:19:00.580
I'm not done.  I set a card and end my turn.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.520
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:08.710
He already has three monsters with 1900 attack points.  Damn.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.760
I summon Panther Warrior!

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.840
It can't attack unless I tribute another monster.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.320
But it has more attack points than his monsters.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.730
So he can't attack me either.

00:19:24.570 --> 00:19:27.040
Scapegoat?  Okay!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:30.940
I set a card and end my turn!

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:35.310
My turn!  I draw!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:37.850
I'll summon this again.

00:19:37.850 --> 00:19:39.580
Pheromone Wasp!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:46.080
I have Obnoxious Celtic Guard on my field.

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:50.860
But Parasite Caterpillar infected it, so it can't defend.

00:19:50.860 --> 00:19:53.860
Take this direct attack!

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.340
Yugi!

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.920
When Pheromone Wasp attacks you directly...

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:15.090
...at the end of the Battle Phase, I can Special Summon a Level 4 or lower Insect from my deck!

00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:21.430
Due to Pheromone Wasp's effect, I Special Summon Leghul!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:30.570
And I activate the Continuous Spell, Insect Barrier!

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:40.010
As long as it's active, your Insects can't attack.

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:46.620
But Yugi doesn't have any Insects on his field.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:56.590
Your infected monster transforms into Poison Butterfly - a giant Insect - in three turns!

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:57.200
What?

00:20:57.200 --> 00:21:02.840
And it shaves 500 life points every turn.

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:06.720
But Poison Butterfly has 2700 attack points.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:10.220
I don't want it to attack me.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:12.910
So I'm preparing in advance.

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.650
I end my turn.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:20.990
Insector Haga is much stronger than before.

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:23.290
Is this due to the Orichalcos?

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.030
But...

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.010
Just wait, partner!

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:29.560
I promise to save you!

00:21:30.210 --> 00:21:32.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:08.550
The streets flow by, colored in red

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:16.960
If you notice your pain, it changes to joy

00:22:18.620 --> 00:22:28.050
People learn of friendship every time they wipe their tears

00:22:28.660 --> 00:22:37.570
With the warm strength you gave me, I'll change them into kindness

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:46.600
My overflowing emotions don't stop

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:52.110
I'll live feeling them

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:57.290
For me to be me

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:05.750
Overflowing friendship heals me

00:23:06.430 --> 00:23:11.390
Our chance meeting was real

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:21.120
We'll both understand that someday

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:30.760
Insector Haga awaited Yugi on top of a runaway train.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:35.360
And Dinosaur Ryuzaki challenged Jonouchi, who was separated from us.

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:40.730
With decks powered up by Doma, they corner Yugi and Jonouchi.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:44.930
Yugi is in no condition to duel composed!

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:48.670
Calm down, Yugi!  Don't let Haga provoke you!

00:23:48.670 --> 00:23:52.450
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Power Up Deck!
Haga & Ryuzaki

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:53.920
Duel, standby!
